velopers we are over 1,000  proprietary algorithms or dynamic  pricing or supply chain management  optimization so we make value chains  very efficient up to full automation and  so far we've been working with very  large corporations we have companies in  almost any industry and last year we  decided to enter the blockchain  community and connect our artificial  intelligence solutions with blockchain  because it makes a lot of sense that  maybe I will tell you later a little bit  about this and then we discovered that  we realize that these technologies we  are connecting and by the way they are  call I'm calling them the new digital  alphabet ABC somehow too good to be true  so a like artificial intelligence or  algorithms be like law chaining see like  cryptocurrency and all we connect all  together these three technologies and  can't make them available to very small  entrepreneurs even to start the  companies to become very efficient and  very competitive against the big guys so  that's something probably you would like  to know to know more in a while well I'd  like to go in the direction to find out  a little bit about your philosophy on  artificial intelligence in the last  three to five years we've seen  everything from basically whole cloth  acceptance of AI all the way to very  very stark warnings about artificial  intelligence in the context of jobs and  employment as well as even more broadly  you know fears about artificial  intelligence becoming self-aware and  evil to some degree to sort of character  characterize it what's your view about  what's your philosophy I guess about  artificial intelligence in the context  of employment of humans yes my idea is  very similar to nah  other people's idea and so I'm very much  convinced that in two to three decades  from now robots and artificial  intelligence will run almost any  business this is happening it is  happening quicker faster and faster and  so the question is as a society we will  have 10 billio